questions.solution_text:
For $x < 0$, sketch $y = x + 4$ as a leftward ray of slope $1$, passing through $(-4,0)$ and ending with an open circle at $(0,4)$.
For $x \ge 0$, sketch $y = 4 - 2x$ as a rightward ray of slope $-2$, starting with a filled dot at $(0,4)$ and passing through $(2,0)$.
The filled dot covers the open circle at the join.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-5.5,0) -- (3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.5) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\node[below] at (-4,0) {$-4$};
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[left] at (0,4) {$4$};
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <-] (-5,-1) -- (0,4);
\draw[thick, ->] (0,4) -- (3,-2);
\fill (0,4) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

questions.question_text:
The graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-3.5,0) -- (3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.5) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <-] (-3,3) -- (0,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[thick, ->, domain=0:2, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {\x*\x + 1});
\draw[fill=white] (0,1) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which piecewise rule matches the given graph?

The graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-3.5,0) -- (3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.5) -- (0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <-] (-3,-2) -- (-1,-2);
\draw[thick] (-1,-2) -- (1,2);
\draw[thick, ->] (1,2) -- (3,2);
\fill (-1,-2) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (1,2) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the range of $f(x)$?
